course: dictionary
lesson: 13231
title: A word from the courtroom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gavel is a small wooden hammer. Judges, auctioneers and chairpeople bang it to get people's attention, to keep order, or to show that something has been decided or sold.
explain: Use the words around gavel to work out its meaning. «The judge banged the gavel, and the room fell silent.» People go quiet after a loud bang, so the gavel must make a sharp, loud sound.
explain: «The auctioneer lifted her gavel and called, "Going, going, gone!" The old painting was sold.» Here the bang means the sale is finished. Check by swapping in the meaning: "The auctioneer lifted her small wooden hammer" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A gavel is a small wooden hammer.
fact: Judges, auctioneers and chairpeople use a gavel to get attention and keep order.
fact: «The gavel came down» means something has been decided or sold.
fact: In British courts judges do not usually use a gavel, but auctioneers do.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland the King of Hearts is the judge at a noisy, silly trial, and a gavel is the kind of tool a judge would use.
exercise: «The judge hit the gavel on the desk, and the room went quiet.» What is a gavel? | A little wooden box | A tiny bell for ringing | A long wooden stick for walking | *A small wooden hammer
exercise: «The auctioneer brought the gavel down, and the vase was sold.» What does the bang of the gavel show? | It shows the auction is closed for lunch | It shows the room is too hot | It shows the vase is broken | *It shows the vase has been sold
exercise: Which people might use a gavel? | A baker and a builder | A nurse and a farmer | *A judge, an auctioneer or a chairperson | A pilot and a driver
test: «The chairperson banged the gavel to get everyone's attention.» Why did she bang the gavel? | To cook dinner | To mend a broken chair | *To get everyone's attention | To wake the dog up
test: «The judge raised the gavel, and everyone stopped talking.» What does the gavel do in this sentence? | It is used to paint the wall | It is used to open the door | It is used to cut bread | *It is used to keep order
exam: «The gavel came down, and the old clock was sold.» What does the gavel show? | It shows the room is empty | *It shows something has been decided or sold | It shows the clock is broken | It shows the clock needs winding
